<div class="wrap narrow">
  <header class="page-head"><h1>About</h1></header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>enihongo is a free website for learning Japanese. Short lessons, usable on a phone. The site is available in Vietnamese and English.</p>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No account needed. Your progress is saved in your browser and can be downloaded as a backup.</li>
      <li>A light static site with no ads and no tracking cookies.</li>
      <li>Visits are counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which uses no cookies and does not track individuals.</li>
      <li>Once a page has been opened you can read it again offline.</li>
      <li>All content is written by the project.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Data sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Stroke order: <a href="http://kanjivg.tagaini.net">KanjiVG</a> by Ulrich Apel, licensed <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>. The selected data lives in <code>data/strokes.json</code> and <code>data/strokes-katakana.json</code> and keeps this license.</li>
      <li>Font Zen Maru Gothic: SIL OFL license.</li>
      <li>Pronunciation: uses the Japanese voice already on your device, so quality depends on the device.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Roadmap</h2>
    <p>The Hiragana basics and Katakana courses are open now. Elementary grammar and vocabulary, basic kanji, conversation and listening will follow.</p>
    <p>The source code is public on <a href="{{ site.repo }}">GitHub</a>. Send feedback and bug reports through Issues.</p>
  </div>
</div>
